      "location": "<article> <div class=\"poem\"> <p> (final two lines)",
      "severity": "minor",
      "source_quote": "Lying to yourself is a foolish thing—\n    “Freedom, or bondage?” is the question I bring.",
      "suggested_fix": "Translate the second line to convey the sense of the speaker 'bringing' or 'posing' the question, and make the phrasing idiomatic in Russian. For example: «Врать себе — глупо и напрасно —\n    «Свобода или рабство?» — вот вопрос, который я выношу.» Preserve the poem tags and line breaks.",
      "translation_quote": "Врать себе — глупо и пусто — так и быть:\n    «Свобода или рабство?» — вот вопрос, что нести."
    },
    {
      "location": "<article> <div class=\"poem\"> <p> (third stanza)",
      "severity": "minor",
      "source_quote": "The bills pile up for comforts and ease;",
      "suggested_fix": "Use a Russian word that preserves 'ease' (comfort and ease) rather than 'лени' (laziness), which shifts the meaning. For example: «Счета растут ради удобств и покоя;» Keep tags and punctuation.",
      "translation_quote": "Счета растут ради удобств и лени; "
